<p>Another difference ➡ <strong>attributes</strong></p>
<ul>
<li data-marpit-fragment="1">
<p>In GIS, the <strong>layer</strong> has one or many <strong>fields</strong>, defining all features in this specific layer</p>
</li>
<li data-marpit-fragment="2">
<p>In OSM, the <strong>layer</strong> does <strong>not</strong> exist. Each feature is individual and has its own fields.</p>
</li>
</ul>

</section>
</foreignObject></svg><svg data-marpit-svg="" viewBox="0 0 960 720"><foreignObject width="960" height="720"><section id="7" data-paginate="true" data-class="lead gaia" data-header="![height:30px](media/logo/osm_logo.png) ![height:30px](media/heart.png) ![height:30px](media/logo/qgis_letter.png)" data-footer="![height:30px](media/foss4g-2021/logo.jpg) Foss4G - Buenos Aires 2021" data-theme="gaia" data-style="section {
